gtk: vmlab: the guest takes the window's size once, and no menu bar

VMLAB_WINDOW_FIXED_SIZE=first: the window's size is offered to the guest (its width a multiple
of 8, its height even) until the guest's picture comes in that size; from then on nothing more
is offered. The guest so runs at the size the window opened with, drawn a guest pixel to a
window pixel (a picture short of the window by less than those steps is drawn unscaled, not
stretched by a fraction), and a later resize of the window scales it (zoom-to-fit) without
changing the guest's mode. A fixed WxH (0003) is scaled whenever the window is not exactly
that size, which on a 1920x1080 screen is always (the title bar takes 37 rows): soft.
The VMLAB_WINDOW window also opens without QEMU's menu bar, whose rows the guest gets
(Ctrl+Alt+M shows it; VMLAB_WINDOW_MENUBAR keeps it).

--- a/system/vl.c
+++ b/system/vl.c
@@ -1398,6 +1398,9 @@
         dpy_window.gl = DISPLAY_GL_MODE_OFF;
         dpy_window.u.gtk.has_zoom_to_fit = true;
         dpy_window.u.gtk.zoom_to_fit = true;
+        /* no menu bar (Ctrl+Alt+M shows it): its rows are the guest's; VMLAB_WINDOW_MENUBAR keeps it */
+        dpy_window.u.gtk.has_show_menubar = true;
+        dpy_window.u.gtk.show_menubar = g_getenv("VMLAB_WINDOW_MENUBAR") != NULL;
